<!-- drawable/ic_battery_wear.xml

     Battery wear profile: a battery holding the screen's own chart.

     Currently UNREFERENCED. It was drawn for the Settings row while that row sat
     under System, where a tile with no icon renders with no icon gutter at all
     and its title breaks the page's alignment. Moving the row to Battery - where
     no row has an icon - made it unnecessary. Kept for if it ever moves back.

     The three bars are the "Charge cycle distribution" the activity actually
     draws - horizontal pills, left-aligned, growing towards the bottom, matching
     the real shape of the data (this device charges mostly from a high state of
     charge, so the bottom buckets are the long ones). A plain battery would have
     said nothing the row's title doesn't already say.

     Body outer (6,4)-(18,22) r=2 with a 1.5 stroke, so the cavity is
     (7.5,5.5)-(16.5,20.5) and the bars sit 0.75 clear of it; the cap overlaps
     into the body's top stroke so the two union cleanly rather than seaming.
     Inner corners r=1 against the outer r=2 to stay concentric.

     Beware the straight runs: a rounded rect's edge must stop a RADIUS short of
     the corner (inner left edge x=7.5 means the bottom run ends at 8.5, not 7.5).
     Getting that wrong silently narrows the stroke on two sides only - it cost a
     round here, and the check is to scan the rendered bitmap rather than trust
     the path: at y=13 the sides must measure 6.0-7.5 and 16.5-18.0.
-->
